   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I have a selectInput element, for example like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inputId</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;si&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> choices</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">letters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> selectize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multiple</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>When I select first &#39;c&#39; then (with Ctrl pressed) &#39;b&#39; I get as result in input$si c(&#39;b&#39;, &#39;c)&#39;. Since I have selected &#39;c&#39; first I would like to get c(&#39;c&#39;,&#39;b&#39;) back. Is this possible without analyzing the input myself?<br><br>Thanks in advance<br><br>Sigbert   <br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "jLvUsLJXBgAJ",
   "from": "Dean Attali",
   "author": "a1bf76ab9a5a2d4b",
   "date": "2017-02-06T05:12:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: selectInput return",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>If you use `selectize = TRUE` then you do get the order in which values were selected. You probably knew that already though since you explicitly want `selcetize=FALSE`.</div><div><br></div><div>In that case you&#39;re just using the default select input that is generated by the browser. And from my experience and from some very limited research, it seems that browsers send the value in the order of rendering. <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/10446796/order-of-selection-in-html-select-multiple\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/10446796/order-of-selection-in-html-select-multiple&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390708236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2keiK2_GStIv7X-POoH-uD\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/10446796/order-of-selection-in-html-select-multiple</a></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>On Thursday, 2 February 2017 03:16:17 UTC-5, Sigbert Klinke  wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I have a selectInput element, for example like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inputId</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;si&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> choices</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">letters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> selectize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multiple</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>When I select first &#39;c&#39; then (with Ctrl pressed) &#39;b&#39; I get as result in input$si c(&#39;b&#39;, &#39;c)&#39;. Since I have selected &#39;c&#39; first I would like to get c(&#39;c&#39;,&#39;b&#39;) back. Is this possible without analyzing the input myself?<br><br>Thanks in advance<br><br>Sigbert   <br></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
