   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>Nope, I did not know this. The reason for the `selectize=FALSE` is that I want a selection box like in <a href=\"https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%C3%BCstruktur_Opera.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%25C3%25BCstruktur_Opera.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390708236000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZOVXDVbJljdhQfgBQMVSb\">https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%C3%BCstruktur_Opera.png</a> rather than some drop down structure to select. Maybe I have to rethink this.<br><br>Nevertheless thanks<br><br>Sigbert</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mXW-kldhBgAJ",
   "from": "Dean Attali",
   "author": "a1bf76ab9a5a2d4b",
   "date": "2017-02-06T08:09:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: selectInput return",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">FYI if you want a dropdown like that, specifically where you can have &quot;groups&quot; of options, you can do that by using a named list as the choices:<div><br></div>  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;select&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;select&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> choices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">`Group A`</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;choice a1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;choice a2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">`Group B`</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;choice b1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;choice b2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div><br><br>On Monday, 6 February 2017 02:59:26 UTC-5, Sigbert Klinke  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>Nope, I did not know this. The reason for the `selectize=FALSE` is that I want a selection box like in <a href=\"https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%C3%BCstruktur_Opera.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%25C3%25BCstruktur_Opera.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390708237000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nmJyD_hiJegAYGHvcFADI\">https://wiki.selfhtml.org/wiki/Datei:Auswahllisten_Men%C3%BCstruktur_Opera.png</a> rather than some drop down structure to select. Maybe I have to rethink this.<br><br>Nevertheless thanks<br><br>Sigbert</div></blockquote></div></div>"
